# Python virtual environment -- large, and fully regeneratable with
# python -m venv venv + pip install, never worth tracking in git.
venv/

# Python bytecode cache -- auto-generated, never needed in version control.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Trained model weights -- binary files, regeneratable by re-running
# train.py / finetune.py. Git handles large binary files poorly (repo
# size balloons, diffs are meaningless), so these are excluded by
# default. Remove this line if you specifically want checkpoints
# version-controlled instead.
#
# Written as checkpoints/* (not checkpoints/) so the exception below
# can un-ignore one file inside it -- git never looks at negation
# patterns for anything inside a directory that's excluded outright.
checkpoints/*

# Exception: the shipped fine-tuned checkpoint IS tracked, unlike the
# rest of checkpoints/ above. It is small (~1.7MB) and, unlike the
# MNIST-only checkpoint, it is NOT trivially regeneratable elsewhere --
# finetune.py needs invoice_digits/, which is real business data that
# is deliberately never pushed to git (see below). Without this file
# committed, a fresh clone (e.g. a cloud coding session) has no way to
# read an invoice at all.
!checkpoints/digit_cnn_finetuned.pt

# Public MNIST data -- large-ish, and trivially re-downloaded any time
# via the curl command already documented for data.py.
data/

# Real invoice photos and the labeled digit crops derived from them --
# actual bakery business/customer data. Excluded by default, not just
# for repo size, but because this is real business data that
# shouldn't end up sitting in a git history, which is genuinely hard
# to fully remove later, especially if this repo is ever pushed
# anywhere shared.
invoices/
invoice_digits/
*.pdf

# Per-invoice extraction output: results.json plus a cropped image of
# every Qty/Return cell. Regenerable from a scan with
# extract_invoice.py, and it is the same real business data as the
# scans it is cut from, so it is excluded for both reasons above.
extractions/

# Individual digit crops banked by review_screen.py's Approve step,
# once a reviewer has confirmed a field was read correctly -- see
# CLAUDE.md, "Banking verified-correct crops as future training data".
# Same reasoning as invoice_digits/ above: real business paperwork,
# and regenerable (by re-approving invoices) rather than a one-off.
digit_bank/

# Verification preview saved by calibrate_total_price.py -- a crop of
# real handwriting off the reference scan, regenerated fresh every time
# that script runs, so it's the same "real business data, regenerable"
# case as invoices/ and extractions/ above.
total_price_calibration_preview.png

# OS-generated junk files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor/IDE workspace settings -- personal preference, not shared project config
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code's local, per-machine permission approvals -- not meant
# to be shared or synced between machines or people.
.claude/settings.local.json
